{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02371",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.29,
      "end_seconds": 5.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.94,
      "end_seconds": 10.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.51,
      "end_seconds": 18.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Um, mainly I've been getting puffed climbing stairs. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.46,
      "end_seconds": 21.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.25,
      "end_seconds": 26.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "I'm on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.07,
      "end_seconds": 30.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.72,
      "end_seconds": 35.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Oh, I've had it for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.24,
      "end_seconds": 50.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "So, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.51,
      "end_seconds": 68.47,
      "duration_seconds": 15.96,
      "text": "It happens all the time. I'd give it a seven, out of ten. Resting helps a bit. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. Oh, and a bit of a cough with exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.86,
      "end_seconds": 72.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.6,
      "end_seconds": 77.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "It happens a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, wheeze or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.0,
      "end_seconds": 90.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.7,
      "end_seconds": 94.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.07,
      "end_seconds": 97.0,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.67,
      "end_seconds": 101.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.77,
      "end_seconds": 105.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "My mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.67,
      "end_seconds": 121.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.14,
      "end_seconds": 131.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Yeah, I have heart disease, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.41,
      "end_seconds": 137.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart disease in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.74,
      "end_seconds": 147.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.38,
      "end_seconds": 152.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.76,
      "end_seconds": 155.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.73,
      "end_seconds": 159.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.3,
      "end_seconds": 163.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.83,
      "end_seconds": 169.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.18,
      "end_seconds": 179.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.11,
      "end_seconds": 184.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Yes, trimethoprim, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.86,
      "end_seconds": 188.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.7,
      "end_seconds": 200.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.69,
      "end_seconds": 228.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.88,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.7 degrees, SpO2 99 percent on room air. And respiratory rate 15, BP is 124 over 68, pulse is 81 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.17,
      "end_seconds": 230.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.34,
      "end_seconds": 241.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly. So, based on your history, the most likely explanation is breathlessness from low fitness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.82,
      "end_seconds": 245.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Um, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.56,
      "end_seconds": 267.15,
      "duration_seconds": 20.59,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now breathlessness from low fitness is my leading thought, not anything worse. Just to be sure I understood. You've been getting puffed climbing stairs for about two weeks, and no chest pain or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.06,
      "end_seconds": 273.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Uh, um, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.09,
      "end_seconds": 302.5,
      "duration_seconds": 18.41,
      "text": "Let's book a peak flow to look into exertional cough. Build up to thirty minutes of brisk walking five days a week. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.63,
      "end_seconds": 305.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.8,
      "end_seconds": 312.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Book a review in eight weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.84,
      "end_seconds": 315.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}